# Intermediates from generate_icon.py / generate_feature_graphic.py.
# Tracked: the three icon masters, the feature graphic, and everything they derive
# (see generate_assets.py). Everything below is reproducible on demand:
#     python store-assets/generate_assets.py --render
preview-*.png
study-*.png
thumb-*.png
icon-play-512.png
ic_launcher_round-192.png

# Android adaptive-icon layers. Rendered, correct, and deliberately NOT shipped: the app
# uses legacy mipmaps only. See issue #150 — the adaptive icon was removed because its
# foreground was an 832-command VectorDrawable that crashed on inflate, not because
# adaptive icons are unwanted. These PNG layers have no such problem, so enabling them is
# a real option (it is what stops Android 8+ launchers shrinking the icon onto a white plate).
adaptive-*.png
